Attorney General William bar says he is  not convinced by his own watchdogs  review of the investigation to the Trump  campaigns ties to Russia the Justice  Department inspector general found the  FBI was justified in opening the  investigation and found no evidence of  political bias but the report did find  that the agents made a series of errors  Catherine Harridge has read the report  now and has more details for us  Catherine good morning to you House  response playing out so far well Gail  the report matters now because of its  political implications and there's  enough in it for both sides to claim  they were right Republicans say this  report exposes wrongdoing by the FBI and  Democrats say it proves the  investigation was legitimate  it's everything that a lot of people  thought it would be except far worse  president Trump was quick to seize on  some of the report's findings they  fabricated evidence and they lied to the  courts and they did all sorts of things  to have it go their way the nearly 440  page Justice Department report found  significant inaccuracies and omissions  in all of the surveillance warrant  applications for former Trump campaign  aide Carter Page in a statement Paige  called the findings evidence of an  egregious overreach by the intelligence  community but the report also found no  documentary or testimonial evidence that  political bias drove the FBI's  decision-making inspector general  Michael Horowitz said the FBI was on  solid ground when it opened the July  2016 counterintelligence probe into  alleged coordination between the Trump  campaign and Russia there are actions  described in this report that I consider  unacceptable and unrepresentative FBI  director Christopher Rea acknowledged  FBI personnel made significant mistakes  but agree with the major findings saying  there was no quote deep state conspiracy  that's not a term I would ever use to  describe our work force and I think it's  an affront to them but in a division  within the department his boss attorney  general bar disputed the findings saying  the investigation into the Trump  campaign was launched on the thinnest of  suspicions and there was an interesting  twist that came out of the report and it  has to do with Christopher Steele if you  remember Steele compiled that in  dossier with unproven details that the  President and Republicans have  repeatedly attacked according to the  report Steele told the inspector general  that before he began his research he was  favorably disposed towards the Trump  family and even had a personal  relationship believed to be with Ivanka  Trump the report did criticize the FBI's  reliance on Steele's dossier which was  used by agents to justify parts of the  investigation  saying much of its information Anthony  was uncorroborated very interesting  Catherine thank you
 

